From 27b632dd401d6a67307820e850beb002a33b7da9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: p104-builder-C <builderC@z4-p104.local>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 02:51:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 15/20] p104 c7a: Pascal dp4a MMQ K-quant inner loops without
 int scale multiplies and quarter-rate conversions

Q4_K/Q5_K/Q6_K dp4a vec_dot: dp4a sums start at 0x4B400000 so the int->float conversion is one FADD,
scale products (d*sc, dmin*m, d6*sc) are floats hoisted per row, results accumulate straight into sum[].
Q4_K/Q5_K: q8_1 (d, s) half2 converted once per block to a float2 smem area (J*4 float2) during the y copy.
GGML_P104_MMQ_LOG=1 logs the tile instance per shape. Q4_K J=64 inner loop SASS 666 -> 532 instr
(I2F+F2F 72 -> 12, XMAD 96 -> 4), regs 114/119/113, no spills.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012TpXXDHrEGeRebppicRic6
